 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Victoria's unemployment rate is higher.** In September 2026 (seasonally adjusted), it was **5.1%** in Victoria and **4.7%** in NSW, a gap of about **0.3 percentage points** (0.34 points unrounded).\n\nVictoria has been above NSW for most of the past year. The gap was narrower in October 2025, when NSW was 4.2% and Victoria was 4.7%.",
